"What counts: total area (land plus inland water such as lakes and rivers) of each sovereign country, as reported in the UN Demographic Yearbook 2024 (Sudan, missing there: World Bank/FAO), cross-checked with the CIA World Factbook. Not counted: Antarctic claims and territories the UN lists separately (Greenland, French overseas regions, Western Sahara; with it Morocco would rank 39th). Disputed areas follow each country's UN figure: India's includes all of Kashmir it claims, Pakistan's excludes the parts it administers, Ukraine is within its recognised borders."